        "notes": "verdict=minor-revision. referee_argument: As a remark interpreting thm:wedderburn-mass-formula the block is the right kind, but its central sentence (md:13-17) presents β_2 = -2[3]_q as 'determined' by an undefined amplitude ratio A_2/A_3 and 'arising' from a classical pair-count C(3,2)=3 'deformed to' [3]_q. The argument conflates color-channel count with pair count (both =3 classically), supplies no rule for the q-deformation, and leaves the -2 factor without in-block provenance. The strongest objection is da-non-sequitur/da-hidden-dof: the [3]_q and the -2 are read off to match the mass formula rather than derived. Recommend re-scoping the prose to 'interprets the degree-2 weight -2[3]_q (derived in thm:wedderburn-mass-formula) as pairwise color binding' and defining A_2/A_3, or pointing to where the deformation rule and -2 are proved."
